# ssh configuration for the dev container. Symlinked to ~/.ssh/config by
# devcontainer.json's postCreateCommand; the host's own ~/.ssh/config is not
# mounted at all, which is the point.
#
# The container has exactly one GitHub identity. `id_container` is whichever
# host key docker-compose.yml binds to that path - `${NEO7DEV_SSH_KEY}`,
# default `neo7_github` - so nothing here names a key, a path on the host,
# or an account. The sibling hextra checkout carries this same file pointing at
# the same key through its own variable.
#
# Both spellings resolve to the same identity on purpose. `origin` uses the
# `github.com-neo7` alias so that the host, which keeps its own multi-key
# config, still selects the right key for the same URL; and a bare
# `ssh -T git@github.com` inside the container answers as the same account
# rather than as whatever the host's default key happens to be.
#
# `IdentitiesOnly yes` is what makes this exclusive. `IdentityFile` alone is a
# preference: the forwarded agent still offers every key it holds and GitHub
# accepts the first that maps to an account. It does not bypass the agent -
# signing still happens there, which is what unlocks a passphrase-protected
# key - it just narrows the offer to this one identity.
Host github.com github.com-neo7
  HostName github.com
  User git
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_container
  IdentitiesOnly yes
